Subject: [PATCH] wifi: retain wrapper ABI after init_dummy_netdev became void

The initializer cannot fail. Call it separately and return zero so the
exported MTK wrapper keeps its existing int signature on both kernel APIs.

--- a/mt_wifi/os/linux/mt_linux.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/os/linux/mt_linux.c
@@ -198,7 +198,8 @@
 
 int mt_init_dummy_netdev(struct net_device *dev)
 {
-	return init_dummy_netdev(dev);
+	init_dummy_netdev(dev);
+	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL(mt_init_dummy_netdev);
 
